<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-=
style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Monday</strong></em> | Our live coverage =
for the week begins at 9am (all times BST) as our cricket writers bring you=
 over-by-over updates on day two of South Africa v Australia in the second =
men=E2=80=99s Test at St George=E2=80=99s Park in Gqeberha.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-=
style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Tuesday</strong></em> | We have two crick=
et offerings starting at 9am, with the first men=E2=80=99s ODI between Paki=
stan and England in the Tri Nations series at the Rawalpindi Cricket Stadiu=
m and the third day of South Africa v Australia. At 8pm the Champions Leagu=
e takes centre stage and we will have minute-by-minute reports on Mancheste=
r City v AEK and Liverpool v Villarreal to keep you company.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-=
style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Wednesday </strong></em>| We go one bette=
r on Wednesday, bringing you three Champions League offerings: Como v Manch=
ester United at 5.45pm, a mouthwatering match as Bayern Munich host Arsenal=
 at 8pm, and a clockwatch with the goals from all the other matches at the =
same time. Before all that, we will be online with day-four coverage of the=
 second men=E2=80=99s Test between South Africa and Australia from 9am.</p>
