Sri Lanka and England as the Tri-Nations Series continues at 9am. And if it=
 gets that far, we will bring you day-five over-by-over updates on the seco=
nd Test between South Africa and Australia at the same time. At 5.45pm buck=
le up for Europa League goal updates as our clockwatch runs all the way thr=
ough until the final whistle blows on the 8pm games.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-=
style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Friday</strong></em> | It is football all=
 the way on Friday, with our live news blog running from 9am to 6pm before =
our minute-by-minute report on the weekend=E2=80=99s first Premier League g=
ame: Ipswich v Nottingham Forest (8pm).</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-=
style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Saturday</strong></em> | We are up and at=
 it from 8am with Matchday Live, bringing you news, discussion and all the =
buildup before the day=E2=80=99s football matches. At 12.30pm Manchester Ci=
ty face what could be another hostile atmosphere as they travel to Aston Vi=
lla =E2=80=93 we will have minute-by-minute updates. Our clockwatch will br=
ing you all the goals from the WSL, Premier League and beyond, also at 12.3=
0pm. Our 5.30pm offering is a London derby as Chelsea host a Tottenham team=
 still looking for a first league win. We focus on F1 at 10pm and lap-by-la=
p updates on the qualifying session for the US Grand Prix.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-=
style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Sunday</strong></em> | Our over-by-over r=
eport on the second men=E2=80=99s ODI between Pakistan and England in the T=
ri Nations series gets under way at 8am, while at the same time Matchday Li=
ve kicks off the day=E2=80=99s football coverage. AT 2pm we=E2=80=99ll have=
 a Premier League clockwatch featuring four games, including Liverpool v Br=
ighton and Manchester United v Bournemouth. Sunderland v Leeds is our bespo=
ke Premier League minute-by-minute report at 4.30pm before the day=E2=80=99=
s biggest match, Barcelona v Real Madrid, which we will bring you live upda=
tes on from 8pm. Away from the football, we=E2=80=99ll have an NFL clockwat=
ch on the 6pm matches and lap-by-lap coverage of F1=E2=80=99s US Grand Prix=
 at 10pm. Be sure to join us.</p>
